# VALIDATION SMOKE for harbor-miles AND the untested 128k layout (coordinator 08:30): 27b-2n-128k (8-GPU TP4 x CP2 headwise
# trainer, 65536 tok/GPU, expandable segments for the trainer; 2 TP4 engines on node 1), 2 LONG de4 tasks x 4, 2 steps.
#  - cell-composition-confounded-estimand: base pass (27B, 128k cap) final context median ~130k, 3/4 sessions hit 128k -> full
#    128k training samples (the trainer's memory edge);
#  - depth-asymmetry-artifact: final context median ~101k (2 of 3 sessions > 96k), the shortest wall time among the long tasks.
#  Decode ~73-100k tokens/session: ~15-25 min each on lightly loaded TP4 engines (base-pass walls of 59-75 min ran on KV-bound
#  TP2 engines), so the agent timeout is 1800 s. 16 in flight = both steps' sessions at once (8 per engine, KV ~0.9M of 1.8M).
# Pass: config line + Miles args as dry-rendered; sandboxes on both nodes; trainer peak memory on 128k samples (expect ~68 GB,
#   STACK §13) for 2 train steps; weight sync to node 1; TITO critical 0; nan_* 0; no OOM. Per node, the agent-server log shows
#   "cancel-file trigger: watching" and "memory watchdog: ... limit ... kill threshold 80%" (sandbox memory safety, aeeb03d7), and a
#   sandbox log shows the ulimit -d cap if logged. Expected ~75-90 min incl. ~20 min setup/JIT (+ ~5 min: the new Harbor patch
#   hash rebuilds the Harbor venv once per cluster).
RUN_NAME=hm-smoke-27b-2n-128k
LAYOUT_PRESET=27b-2n-128k
DATASET=de4-v1-k1
TASK_IDS_FILE=${HM_EXAMPLE_DIR}/configs/tasks/de4-smoke2-long.txt
CAP=128k
RBS=2
NS=4
NUM_ROLLOUT=2
ASYNC_CONCURRENCY=16
DROP_ZERO_STD=0
HM_AGENT_TIMEOUT=1800
HM_CHAIN_MAX=0
